  "NROOT" [label="(0,0,0) This paper motivates, develops, and evaluates a strategy that combines bulky amide solvent SDAs with mixed Im/bIm ligands to create meltable, large-pore ZIF-derived MOF glasses and free-standing membranes for improved gas separation and CO2-capture-related applications.", fillcolor="lightyellow", style="filled"];
  "NROOT_COMMON" [label="(0,0,0) Together, the retained and repaired conclusions move from application motivation, through MOF-glass feasibility and porosity-preservation design, to evaluation of porous MOF-glass membranes for gas-separation applications."];
  "R1" [label="(0,0,0) Climate change driven by excessive energy consumption and fossil-fuel burning motivates research into technologies that address greenhouse-gas and CO2 emissions."];
  "R11" [label="(0,0,0) Reduction of inherent porosity during glass formation explains why MOF glasses face a porosity challenge for gas-separation applications."];
  "R12" [label="(0,0,0) The difficulty of precise Ångstrom-scale porosity manipulation in MOF glasses motivates exploring porosity-enhancement strategies such as pore-inducing agents."];
  "R14" [label="(0,0,0) Because ligand-directed use of large ligands is not applicable to meltable MOFs and extra ligands may lower decomposition temperature, porosity enhancement without extra ligands is motivated."];
  "R15" [label="(0,0,0) Using SDAs without extra ligands is a plausible strategy for creating highly porous topologies while maintaining meltability."];
  "R16" [label="(0,0,0) For pure Im-based CAN and AFI ZIFs, recrystallization to dense ZIF-zni before melting indicates that suppressing recrystallization is important for preserving porosity in melt-quenched glass."];
  "R17" [label="(0,0,0) Using mixed Im and bIm ligands can suppress recrystallization to a dense phase and preserve porosity."];
  "R18" [label="(0,0,0) Bulky amide solvents used as SDAs support formation of highly porous topologies without extra ligands."];
  "R19" [label="(0,0,0) Mixed Im and bIm ligands are a porosity-preserving component because they suppress recrystallization to dense phases."];
  "R2" [label="(0,0,0) Carbon-capture research is an active and motivated direction for reducing CO2 emissions."];
  "R20" [label="(0,0,0) When enhanced porosity carries over to glass upon melt quenching with high gas-adsorption capacities, the resulting MOF glasses are expected to support strong gas-separation performance."];
  "R6" [label="(0,0,0) Reported use of large solvent molecules as SDAs supports a bounded strategy in which SDAs can help synthesize large-pore ZIF topologies, including 12-membered-ring examples with large pore apertures."];
  "R8" [label="(0,0,0) A free-standing porous MOF-glass membrane with strong gas-separation performance motivates considering porous MOF glasses for energy-gas purification and CO2-capture applications."];
